  <p>
    One more capability rounds out the picture: <strong>conditional slots</strong>. Because slots
    arrive as props, the layout can <em>choose</em> which one to render - which means one URL can serve
    fully separated experiences. The canonical case is role-based UI:
    <code>@admin</code> and <code>@user</code> are two complete page trees with their own data, loading,
    and error lifecycles, and the layout picks per request. No client-side role branching, and - because
    the choice happens on the server -
    <strong>the admin code never ships to non-admin users</strong>.
    <Chip k='next' />
    <Chip k='very' />
  </p>

