      single round trip. Independent reads on the server go one better: they start the moment the
      request arrives, they run next to the data (short bars), and each region streams into its
      reserved space as it resolves (<a href='11-suspense-streaming.html'>§11</a>). The parallel
      <em>client</em> version is not the same thing wearing a different color: nothing can start until
      the bundle downloads and hydrates (the gray segment), and every read is then a full browser-to-server
      round trip (long bars). Decoupling the queries is still worth it there (the user waits for the slowest,
      not the sum), but the whole lane starts late and travels farther.
