    <Fragment slot='caption'>
      The same three reads, decided by component structure. In the serial lane nobody wrote "wait
      for the previous request"; the nesting wrote it, because each layer's hook can't run until the
      layer above renders it. In the parallel lane the keys were known up front, so every request
      starts the moment hydration finishes, and the region resolves on the slowest request instead
      of the sum.
    </Fragment>
  </Diagram>

  <p>
    So the standing rule for the cases where client fetching is genuinely required (<a
      href='15-dedupe-caching.html#when-client'>§15.7</a
    >): <strong>the client data flow must never be serial.</strong> If you find a request that can't start
    until another finishes, that is not a fact of life to be styled around with spinners; it is a signal
    that something upstream is shaped wrong. Either the earlier request should
    <strong>fetch more</strong> (return what the children need, so one response feeds the region), or
    the requests should be <strong>re-keyed to what is already known</strong> so they run in parallel,
    or the chain never belonged on the client at all and moves to the server. Serial client data flow
    is a design bug, not a constraint.
  </p>

  <h2 id='rules'>The rules</h2>
  <table class='tbl'>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Rule</th>
        <th>Scope</th>
        <th>Importance</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>
          <strong>Await where the data is used</strong> - the blocking scope of a request is exactly the
          subtree behind the await.
        </td>
        <td><Chip k='react' /></td>
        <td><Chip k='critical' /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          Independent requests run <strong>in parallel</strong> - sibling self-fetching components, or
          <code>Promise.all</code> within one component. Never serialized awaits for unrelated data.
        </td>
        <td><Chip k='react' /></td>
        <td><Chip k='critical' /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          Dependent chains are <strong>confined to the smallest region</strong> that needs their result.
        </td>
        <td><Chip k='react' /></td>
        <td><Chip k='very' /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          Regions deserving route-level independence become
          <strong>parallel-route slots</strong> - own loading, own error, own stream.
        </td>
        <td><Chip k='next' /></td>
        <td><Chip k='very' /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          Parallel routes: every slot defines <strong><code>default.tsx</code></strong> - a hard navigation
          to a URL the slot doesn't match must not 404 the route.
        </td>
        <td><Chip k='next' /></td>
        <td><Chip k='critical' /></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>
          No client-side dependent query chains -
          <strong>resolve dependencies on the server</strong>, or collapse them into one key.
        </td>
        <td><Chip k='react' /></td>
        <td><Chip k='critical' /></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

